                    This distinction also protects honest questioning. Faith seeks understanding and can bring difficulties into prayer, study, and trusted conversation. Doubt can mean different things: an involuntary difficulty, a neglected question, a deliberate refusal, or a season of suffering. An app should not flatten these into a verdict. Hope likewise differs from optimism. Optimism predicts that circumstances will improve; hope trusts God's fidelity and final promise even when the path includes the cross.

                    Charity differs from approval, sentimentality, and conflict avoidance. To love another is to will and act for that person's true good in God. That may require tenderness, boundaries, correction, protection of a victim, forgiveness, or patient accompaniment. Charity never authorizes falsehood or participation in evil. Because it seeks communion in truth, it perfects rather than cancels justice.
