                    Hebrews 11 portrays faith as lived trust across generations, often without immediate fulfillment. Romans 5 joins justification, peace, endurance, tested character, hope, and God's love poured into hearts through the Holy Spirit. The passages prevent us from isolating the three virtues. Faith receives and entrusts; hope stretches toward fulfillment; charity already shares the divine life toward which hope moves.

