                    Because these virtues are gifts, practice is not a technique that forces God to act. Practice makes a human response concrete and disposes the person to remain available. The believer asks for increase in faith, hope, and love, receives sacramental grace, and then brings those gifts into budgets, speech, sexuality, work, conflict, and care.

