                    These should not be treated as collectible achievements. Fruit grows from living union. In John 15, branches bear fruit by abiding in the vine. The branch is genuinely fruitful; the fruit appears through its living activity. Yet its life is received. Jesus also joins abiding to commandments and love, so dependence is not inactivity. It becomes a form of obedient communion.

