                    Catholic formation is also social. Sin and virtue affect institutions, customs, workplaces, families, and public life. A privately courteous person may still benefit from unjust arrangements or ignore duties to the poor. The common good asks for social conditions in which persons and communities can flourish. Learning justice therefore includes attention to both face-to-face conduct and the structures shaped by collective choices.

